"The next step was to use my thumbs to create a hole in the center of the clay. As my thumbs pressed gently into the soft clay, the hole gradually took shape. It was important that the hole didn’t go too deep or the pot that I was making would have a hole in the base—a lesson that Luke would later learn the hard way. While my thumbs enlarged the cavity, the heel of my hands held the clay centered and prevented the base from expanding out as I pushed down; in effect, your hands are like a free-form mold.": "02597cb3ff41",
