"When we encountered any of the arachnids, I wanted to instill in the children a sense of awe for the eight-legged creatures and not a sense of fear. We approached them with respect and tried to observe them passively. The last thing we wanted was to disturb the spiders or to make them scared of us. Observing and talking about what we saw was one way for us to understand them more and fear them less. By the way the children were curiously looking at the spiders, I think any fear they had of them had vanished.": "dd855b93da54",
